## Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: single `S` object; `R()`/mulberry32 reads/writes `S.rngState`; `runTurn(s)` calls storm→production→needs→events→caravan→checkEnd in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: `genMap(seed)` produces 64-tile grid from seeded RNG; `tryBuild` checks `d.terr.includes(s.map[i])`; `adjCount` drives condenser/greenhouse/forge output multipliers. Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: chains sifter(ash→soil)→greenhouse(soil+water→food), mine(ore)→forge(ore+power→metal)→workshop(metal+power→parts); `addRes` clamps to `caps()` and logs overflow. Score 2.

**F4 Population**: colonist records `{skill,fatigue,morale,b(job slot)}`; `workerMult(s,c,d)` reads `c.skill`/`c.fatigue`/`c.morale` in `production()`. Score 2.

**F5 Needs**: `needsPhase` consumes food/water per pop, `dm-=12/-10` on shortage, recovery `dm=2+...` when no shortage, feeds `workerMult`. Score 2.

**F6 Research**: 10 nodes in `RESEARCH`; `tryResearch` enforces `node.req.every(has)` and deducts cost; each id (`filters`,`bore`,`drip`,`heatx`,`turbine`,`depots`,`shield`,`barter`,`salvage`,`medbay`) is read in production/caps/storm/trade/needs code. Score 2.

**F7 Events**: 12 entries in `EVENTS`; `eventsPhase` does weighted roll via `e.w`/`total`; 6 events (refugees, wreck, sickness, thieves, trainer, festival) have 2-3 choices with differing `apply`; `s.cds[ev.id]=EVENT_COOLDOWN` filtered from pool. Score 2.

**F8 Trade**: `priceOf` uses `s.res[g]/cap` scarcity and `s.drift[g]` (random-walked in `caravanPhase`); `cv.inv[g]` limits buy qty; `tradeDeal` handles both buy/sell branches. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard**: `stormPhase` fires `turn%8===0`, `sev=1+floor(turn/20)`; `production()` halves output at `hp<50`, disables at `hp<=0`; `shield` research + `wallCount` mitigate; `tryRepair` spends parts+metal+colonist labor. Score 2.

**F10 Save/load**: `exportSave()`→`JSON.stringify(stripUi(S))` into textarea; `importSave` parses JSON, validates required fields/map length/resource types, returns clear error strings. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: `checkEnd` sets lose (`colonists.length===0`) and win (`turn>=60 && pop>=12 && !shortage`); `score(s)` combines pop/research/turn/stockpile; `renderModal` shows breakdown table. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: `switchTab` toggles panels; `renderLog` prefixes `T${e.t}`; title attributes on resbar/tiles explain formulas; Space/1-5 keydown handlers; `@media(max-width:420px)` rules. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests` asserts caps, prereqs, terrain checks, overflow clamp, storm schedule, starvation departures, cooldowns, trade state, save/load hash round-trip, research-vs-production comparison; `runBench` runs 200 headless turns via `greedyTurn`, prints `stateHash`. Score 2.

**G1**: `has(s,"filters")` etc. multiply directly inside `production()` formulas (condenser/mine/ventTap/greenhouse/forge), applied every turn, shown in `b.note`. Score 4.

**G2**: `needsPhase` shortage → `dm` → `c.morale`; `workerMult` reads `c.morale` (<40 ×0.7, ≤0 refuse) feeding into `production()` next cycle. Score 4.

**G3**: `stormPhase` damages `b.hp` → `production()` checks `hp<50`/`hp<=0` → `tryRepair` spends `{parts:2,metal:1}`+idle labor → `hp=100` restores full output. Score 4.

**G4**: `priceOf` reads `s.res[g]/caps(s)[g]` scarcity and `s.drift[g]` (updated every turn in `caravanPhase` via random walk). Score 4.

**G5**: refugees/wreck/thieves/sickness choices call `addColonist`, `spend`, `s.colonists.forEach(morale...)` — real state mutation, not just `logMsg`. Score 4.

